# Advisories hack/ci.sh's npm audit accepts in what ships, each in the one directory and package named, with why, and
# until when: from that date on, the audit reports it again. Any other high or critical advisory fails the stage.
# One line each, the comment above it saying why (hack/lib/npm-audit.py reads them):
#   <directory> <package> <advisory> <expires>

# body-parser 2.3.0, through Express 5.2.1: a compressed body with bytes after its end, a denial of service. The API
# refuses every compressed body before any parser reads it (BE/src/app-setup.ts), and the backend's other servers
# (function URLs, buckets, queues) read their bodies without it: nothing reaches the flaw. Fixed in 2.4.0
# (2026-10-22), two weeks old on 2026-11-05: updated then.
BE body-parser GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828 2026-11-05

# multer 2.4.0, which @nestjs/platform-express 12.1.2 pins: a denial of service through an asynchronous fileFilter
# still pending when the request ends. Multer only runs behind Nest's file interceptors, which the backend uses
# nowhere: nothing reaches it. Fixed in 2.5.0 (2026-10-22), two weeks old on 2026-11-05: an override in
# BE/package.json then, until Nest pins it.
BE multer GHSA-q7qp-rjg7-q26m 2026-11-05
